# What has passed IsClosureOf is what its type shares with the closures of that function, and never more than the type held. A built-in is a closure of no function of the application, so it does not pass. One that is implemented in JavaScript may be a closure of the function the program registers for it, and an instance of Function may be a closure of any function: both may pass, and a refusal takes neither away
